add(52,[85,86],'conjecture',[49],'Pro early 1786–1792; K12-03 326','unirationnelle ??',
 'The page asks whether vanishing of all positive gamma-invariants, in particular entirely algebraic cohomology, forces unirationality.',
 'For i>0 and rational homological motives over C, an Enriques surface has motive 1+10Q(−1)+Q(−2), so all positive bipure pieces vanish while Kodaira dimension0 excludes unirationality. This does not infer a Chow-motive decomposition merely from Betti numbers.',
 'agrees','The i>0 versus i≥0 ink ambiguity and the motivic interpretation are explicit conditions of the counterexample.')
add(53,[87,88,89],'withdrawn in the same text',[50],'Pro early 1796–1816; K12-03 330–335','Non en car. p>0',
 'The quotient of the dimension-graded scissors group by ruled classes is compared with top bipure motives. The consequence that algebraic H2 forces a surface to be ruled is rejected by the author using E×E with E supersingular.',
 'Here b2=6 and all degree2 classes are algebraic, but an abelian surface has no rational curves. Its H1 is nonzero, so it is not an example for vanishing of every positive gamma. Larsen–Lunts concerns a different whole-ring quotient by the affine line.',
 'agrees','The negative answer and its exact scope are in the margin; the broader quotient question is not settled by naming a related theorem.')
add(54,[91],'idea of the earlier run',[],'Pro early notes 816–823; current scans2–50 have no A–D dictionary','No letter definitions on these pages',
 'Compare conjectures by their mathematical content before identifying manuscript A–D labels with printed B,C,D,I labels.',
 'The reported cote16 and other-folder endpoints are absent. Published standard-conjecture texts can be checked, but no missing handwritten letter is reconstructed.',
 'agrees','The partial dictionary remains correctly bounded by its source evidence.')
add(55,[92],'idea of the earlier run',[],'Pro early notes824–831; middle notes63–68','No explicit cote14 continuation here',
 'The earlier notes suggest a connection between the singular-hypersurface programme reported from cote16 and cote14, and the general-base or birational material here.',
 'No actual cote14/16 transcription is attached. Record a contextual lead with unavailable second endpoint, not an archive link independently verified at both places.',
 'agrees','A bounded negative search does not prove the programme was undeveloped.')
add(56,[93],'idea of the earlier run',[59,60,63],'Pro early notes832–839; Pro middle227–255,300–322','On pense; je doute',
 'Modern Nori/Ayoub group comparison, motivated pure comparison, and motivic six operations give different established parts of the old programme.',
 'They do not identify numerical motives with faithful classical realizations, prove all standard conjectures, or establish a universal motivic t-structure. Ayoub’s 2026 anabelian theorem concerns a much richer functor of all varieties.',
 'agrees','Earlier comparisons are retained only with their exact coefficient/base and category hypotheses.')
add(57,[94],'idea of the earlier run',[5,6,16,17,59],'Pro early140–156,541–600; Pro middle227–255','torseur',
 'Fibre-functor torsors are present. A statement that the Betti–de Rham comparison point is generic in its torsor, or that all numerical period relations are motivic, is not present in the supplied leaves.',
 'The period conjecture is a separate modern comparison. Linear period relations in an abelian subcategory do not settle algebraic relations in its tensor closure.',
 'agrees','Absence is bounded to the supplied full transcriptions and checked Codex leads, not the entire archive.')
add(58,[97],'idea of the earlier run',[13,15,59],'Pro early414–444,486–500; middle227–235','h. scalaires',
 'Separate the centre of a motivic group, its central weight, the scalar/algebraic part of a proposed Lie pro-motive, and centres appearing in prior LM projects.',
 'These have different objects and quantifiers. The final scan59 reading differs materially between Pro’s scalar reading and Codex’s nul with a deleted scalar passage.',
 'agrees','No proof of a vanishing centre is imported through a resemblance of vocabulary.',middle=[17])
add(59,[98],'idea of the earlier run',[74,75,82],'Pro early notes872–879; Pro middle503–546,645–675','Tmotif(A)',
 'Oda’s characteristic-p de Rham/Dieudonné comparison is a relevant structured-realization result, separate from the ell≠p Sha and local-duality arguments.',
 'Use the abelian-variety Corollary5.11 with Frobenius/Verschiebung/Hodge data. The more general proper-smooth Corollary5.12 additionally assumes a rational point.',
 'agrees','The context link is mathematical, not evidence that the manuscript already states Oda’s later theorem.',middle=[63])
add(60,[99,100],'title, date or page count',[11,21,96,97,98],'Pro early325–329,673–714; Pro middle1068–1071; B12-01 140–156','Poids et niveaux; par A.GROTHENDIECK',
 'Archive foliation, author section numbers, scans and physical file lines are different coordinate systems. The scan96 cover and scan97–98 introduction begin a separate weights/levels text; the introduction says the method originated in1964.',
 '1964 is retrospective dating of the method, not a date written for the whole dossier. Early claims that later Hua pages were unavailable are updated where corresponding late Pro/Codex leaves are now attached.',
 'understates','The earlier run’s source boundary is obsolete for attached later leaves; no Hua file or scan image has been supplied.',middle=[61])

